00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:32.170
to

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:19.590
Hi. Have you ever seen one of these? Probably not. They're shackles.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:26.780
400 years ago, millions of African men and women were kidnapped, forced to wear these.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.460
Then they were crammed into the bellies of cargo ships, like this one.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:49.050
It was a cruel and horrible journey.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.300
People were packed end to end, top to bottom.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:58.330
This old drawing of a slave ship shows there was no room to move or breathe.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:01:59.970
Every inch of...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.610
space was packed with human beings. For months, there was no fresh air, no sunshine. Being in this

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:28.710
place, I can almost hear the voices of my kidnapped ancestors. It's so dark down here, hard to breathe.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:46.750
some of us sick some are dead i miss my family my village my home is gone ever once this boat

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:59.780
stops i don't know where i'll be or where i'll be going slave

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.360
Ships landed here, in America, and African people who were once free were sold as property to the highest bidder.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:14.940
That's a one-prime bill. What do I hear?

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:16.290
$500.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.370
$700. I have $900.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:23.170
And $1,000 sold to the man in the green west pit.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:37.460
One of the worst things about slavery is that families were separated.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:42.200
Fathers, mothers, and children were oftentimes sold to different people.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.580
Hell, baby. Into the future, gentlemen.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:48.530
What am I offering?

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.350
It's been many years since they took my boy from me.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.370
It's like yesterday.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.970
Men come to look on us, poking and prodding.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.000
like we was meat.

00:04:02.748 --> 00:04:06.588
I begged and I pleaded, please don't take my child.

00:04:08.732 --> 00:04:10.572
But they pay no mind to my tears.

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:13.228
And my boy, he look at me.

00:04:15.356 --> 00:04:15.556
Let's see.

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:18.384
Good child.

00:04:20.412 --> 00:04:21.612
Good for your mama.

00:04:44.908 --> 00:04:48.088
Being a slave meant you had no freedom to live as you wanted.

00:04:48.684 --> 00:04:48.944
Yeah.

00:04:52.044 --> 00:04:52.704
You were owned.

00:04:52.972 --> 00:04:53.972
by another person.

00:04:54.348 --> 00:04:56.108
and forced to do the hardest.

00:04:56.268 --> 00:04:57.028
dirtiest work.

00:04:58.412 --> 00:04:59.952
We go to them fields.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.560
from sunup to sundown.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:04.910
Tired and thirsty,

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.380
Sunday you're one day a rest.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.030
Even then,

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:12.110
you're at the master's calling.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:21.370
In spite of the hardships, enslaved Africans built new families, new communities.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.620
Traditions were kept alive.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:27.460
Children learned the stories, games and dances of their people.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:29.580
And always,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:38.540
there was the music. Music was the language of their greatest joys and deepest sorrows.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:59.480
Many bore the burden of slavery. They survived.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:04.220
and built their lives on the hope that someday their children would be free.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:14.950
But for others, the hope of some...

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.480
Someday being free was not enough.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.080
I need to be free.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.550
They say I'm not.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.620
We can be free.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:29.340
Can I ask?

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:43.900
best way to escape was under cover of darkness but how could they find their way north at night

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.410
They followed the drinking gourd.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.580
This is a drinking gourd.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:56.620
Here's a bowl for water and a handle for dipping.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.520
It looks just like...

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:13.070
That group of stars in the sky, those stars were called the drinking gourd because it looked just like their water dippers.

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:14.840
You can see the...

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:22.280
and the handle, and there are the two special stars that help point the way north.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:29.850
Escaping slaves sang a song about those stars that led them to freedom.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.730
A song called Follow the Drinking Gourd.

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:41.630
The sun comes back and the first quail calls.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.740
Follow the Drinking Gourd.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:49.840
for the old man is a-waitin' for to carry you to freedom.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.180
Follow the drinking gourd.

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:58.790
Story and Pictures by Jeanette Winter

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.410
Read by Keith David.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.400
Long ago, before the Civil War,

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:13.160
there was an old sailor called Pig-Leg Joe

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:16.790
who did what he could to help free the slaves.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:20.280
Joe had a plan.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:23.820
He'd use hammer and nail and saw

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:25.620
and work for the master,

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.810
the man who owned the slaves on the cotton plantation.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:39.240
At night, when work was done, he'd teach the slaves a song that secretly told the way to freedom.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.500
Just follow the drinking gourd, it said.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:46.160
When the song was learned and sung all day,

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:52.220
Peg Leg Joe would slip away to work for another master and teach the song again.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:59.410
One day, a slave called Molly saw her man James.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:08.110
sold to another master. James would be taken away, their family torn apart. Just one more

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:17.440
night together. Quail called in the trees that night. Molly and James remembered Joe's

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:28.100
song. When the sun comes back and the first quail calls, follow the drinking gourd, for

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.980
the old man is a-waiting for-

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:40.460
to carry you to freedom follow the drinking door they looked to the sky and saw the stars taking

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:51.380
their little son isaiah old hattie and her grandson george molly and james set out for freedom that

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:58.320
very night they ran all night through the fields till they crossed the stream to the woods

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:08.320
daylight came they hid in the trees watching listening for the master's hounds set loose to

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:17.610
find them but the dogs lost the runaway scent at the stream and they were not found they hid all

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:26.240
day in the woods at night they walked again singing joe's song and looking for the signs

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:27.480
that marked the trail.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:29.970
The riverbank...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:39.520
makes a very good road the dead trees will show you the way left foot peg foot traveling on

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:52.460
follow the drinking gore by night sleeping by day for weeks they traveled on they never knew

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:59.810
what lay ahead sometimes empty bellies to sleep on sometimes no stars

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.670
guide the way. There was danger

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:05.160
from men who would send them back.

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:07.650
Danger from hungry beasts.

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.800
But sometimes, a kind deed was

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:14.200
done. One day, a boy brought

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.140
bacon and cornbread to share.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:21.760
Singing low, traveled on.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.960
The river ends between

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.480
two hills. Follow

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:29.320
the drinking gourd.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.620
There's another river on the other side.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.420
Follow the drinking gourd.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.660
When the great big river meets the little river,

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:43.370
follow the drinking gourd.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:47.470
For the old man is a-waiting for to carry you to freedom.

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:51.790
If you follow the drinking gourd...

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.440
They climb the last hill.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:59.960
Down below was Piglet Joe waiting.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.800
at the wide Ohio River to carry them across.

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:10.340
Under a starry sky, Joe rode them across the river.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:14.500
He told them of hiding places where they would be safe.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:21.070
A path of houses stretched like a train on a secret track leading north to Canada.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:24.800
He called it the Underground Railroad.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.960
It carried riders to freedom.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:39.290
first safe house stood on a hill. The lamp was lit, which meant it was safe to come. The door

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:45.630
opened wide to welcome the freedom travelers. Then they were rushed to the barn, for the farmers knew

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:55.360
there would be slave catchers near. Peg Leg Joe went back to the river to meet others who were

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:56.760
following the drinking gourd.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.740
The farmer sent the travelers to the next safe house.

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:09.210
Here, they were led to a secret room hidden behind shelves.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.520
They rested and healed their wounds.

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:21.620
Soft beds, full meals, and hot baths washed away some fear and pain.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:29.980
When they were strong, they traveled again from house to house to house on the underground.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:40.490
brown trail still following the drinking gourd north at last they came to the shores of lake

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:47.780
erie molly and james and isaiah old hattie and young george climbed aboard the steamship and

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:59.880
carry them across to canada freedom five more souls are safe old hattie cried they had followed

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:13.990
the drinking gourd songs like follow the drinking gourd led the way north for many

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:21.970
slaves but music did more for african americans than lead us to freedom it expressed joys and

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:26.230
and sorrows lifted our spirits and gave us hope.

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:34.860
This is Sweet Honey in the Rock.

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:56.960
Today, this group of African-American women sings to keep alive the songs of slavery and the spirit of freedom.

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:29.980
When African people were brought here as slaves, we brought the tradition of

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:36.730
singing as a part of everyday life and making music with us. Music is something

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:40.370
that they can't take away from you. You have your voice, you have your feelings

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:45.580
and quite frankly I don't think we would be here if it wasn't for the music,

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:51.460
for the songs to be able to express how we were feeling. And if you think about

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:56.400
songs that make you feel good, when you feel terrible, when you think oh I feel

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:59.970
I can't feel any worse today and then a song

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.180
comes to you that makes you feel better when you sing it that's exactly what

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:10.500
slaves did when you're sad sometimes you sing a song you could be singing a

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:16.260
sad song and then you feel but you feel better and it gives you the strength to

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:20.160
move through whatever it is that you're going through music is very important in

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:20.380
life

