To the.

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:20.310
Balm and Gilead is a spiritual. Balm, B-A-L-M, is a soothing ointment. And it's a song that talks about a place where there is hope, there's soothing, and there's healing.

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:53.030
you will hear over and over again in songs created during slavery is that you

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:59.910
must go on no matter what you face you go on and if you

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:09.320
find that you are being controlled or enslaved by someone else you're not free to speak openly you

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:14.350
can't tell them exactly what you want them what you want to say and so you have to find other

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:22.510
ways to do it a code song is a song that is familiar to the slaves on the plantation it's

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:28.160
a song that contains a secret message to let everybody who's familiar with the song know that

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:29.610
Tonight is the night.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.700
It's time to keep your ear out for the next message so we can escape to freedom.

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:50.860
The song says, Run, Moana, Run.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:59.980
In this song, the mourner stands for a person enslaved to tell that person.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:16.920
person to run is to say, try to get away. So run Mona, run is a way the community is saying, go ahead, get away and escape.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:34.970
You got to escape for your life

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:44.510
Sometimes escape for your life

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:49.620
You just got to escape for your life

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:51.890
And love and love

